        "original_id": "e2b02f17-8619-5b3c-a4e7-5fc6c1945c95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\", \"Then Who Am I\"\n- People: Dallas Frazier, A.L. \"Doodle\" Owens, Charley Pride, The Oak Ridge Boys\n\nFacts:\n- Fancy Free was the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys and was released on March 26, 1981.\n- In 1981, \"Elvira,\" written by Dallas Frazier, became a famous country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys and is considered one of their signature songs.\n- The songs \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles, but all failed to chart within the top 40.\n- \"Then Who Am I\" was written by Dallas Frazier and A.L. \"Doodle\" Owens and was recorded by American country music artist Charley Pride.",
